1
00:00:00,958 --> 00:00:03,042
You're not going on a date, are you?

2
00:00:03,167 --> 00:00:04,458
With who?

3
00:00:05,208 --> 00:00:06,500
Hmm?

4
00:00:13,083 --> 00:00:15,042
So Sui likes this kind of stuff.

5
00:00:16,542 --> 00:00:18,000
Yeah.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,125
Dai-chan...

7
00:00:24,243 --> 00:00:25,576
What...?

8
00:00:26,375 --> 00:00:29,042
You never used to avoid me like this.

9
00:00:29,458 --> 00:00:31,583
Who are you going on a date with?

10
00:00:31,708 --> 00:00:32,333
Huh?

11
00:00:32,458 --> 00:00:33,833
Ah.

12
00:00:34,208 --> 00:00:35,417
Well... um.

13
00:00:37,917 --> 00:00:39,458
Huh? Harutora?

14
00:00:40,292 --> 00:00:42,250
Hold on... Harutora.

15
00:00:42,375 --> 00:00:43,542
Hey.

16
00:00:46,417 --> 00:00:47,542
Harutora.

17
00:01:04,583 --> 00:01:06,542
Hey... don't be like that.

18
00:01:13,750 --> 00:01:16,500
Why do you let your guard
down around a guy like him?

19
00:01:16,625 --> 00:01:17,667
I'm not...

20
00:01:18,333 --> 00:01:19,476
I didn't mean anything by it.

21
00:01:19,500 --> 00:01:21,250
It sure didn't look that way to me.

22
00:01:21,375 --> 00:01:22,833
I'm serious.

23
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:25,667
I've always thought the way Dai-chan acts...

24
00:01:25,792 --> 00:01:27,708
- is really annoying...
- If that's the case,

25
00:01:28,958 --> 00:01:32,125
Then why did you bring
him into your room before?

26
00:01:32,250 --> 00:01:37,083
That's because a junior... used my
personal honey without knowing it was mine.

27
00:01:37,208 --> 00:01:40,083
And Dai-chan found out.

28
00:01:40,208 --> 00:01:41,667
So that's why...

29
00:01:43,708 --> 00:01:44,875
Forget it.

30
00:01:49,667 --> 00:01:52,292
There's no way to prove
if that's true or not anyway.

31
00:01:54,333 --> 00:01:56,250
That's a bit harsh...

32
00:01:57,125 --> 00:01:58,417
Harutora, you're the one who...

33
00:01:59,917 --> 00:02:02,042
Why didn't you tell me sooner?

34
00:02:03,083 --> 00:02:04,417
Huh?

35
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:07,000
If you didn't like it,

36
00:02:07,125 --> 00:02:08,833
You should've just said so.

37
00:02:10,792 --> 00:02:13,042
Why did you keep it to yourself?

38
00:02:21,833 --> 00:02:23,458
That's because...

39
00:02:26,625 --> 00:02:28,000
What?

40
00:02:32,542 --> 00:02:33,958
Nothing.

41
00:02:36,167 --> 00:02:37,500
Harutora...

42
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:25,808
"Hold on, Harutora-kun"
(Episode 6)

43
00:03:27,417 --> 00:03:28,208
Harutora...

44
00:03:28,333 --> 00:03:29,750
Yeah.

45
00:03:29,875 --> 00:03:30,583
Coming.

46
00:03:30,708 --> 00:03:31,708
Found it, found it!

47
00:03:31,833 --> 00:03:32,708
Sui.

48
00:03:32,833 --> 00:03:34,042
I heard you got a boyfriend.

49
00:03:34,167 --> 00:03:34,708
Huh?

50
00:03:34,833 --> 00:03:35,976
How did you guys get together?

51
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,458
- What?
- Is he older than you?

52
00:03:37,583 --> 00:03:39,059
Don't tell me it's someone from the dorm?

53
00:03:39,083 --> 00:03:40,167
What!?

54
00:03:40,292 --> 00:03:41,476
No, what are you guys talking about?

55
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,500
No, no.

56
00:03:42,542 --> 00:03:44,500
Hold on...

57
00:03:44,625 --> 00:03:46,083
You're going on a date later, right?

58
00:03:46,208 --> 00:03:49,208
And dressed like that, you
look like an inflatible tube man!

59
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:50,476
At least unzip the front, will you?

60
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:52,292
That's enough!

61
00:03:52,417 --> 00:03:53,625
What's wrong?

62
00:03:53,750 --> 00:03:55,934
If you get dumped for dressing
so tacky, don't come crying to me.

63
00:03:55,958 --> 00:03:58,125
I heard relationships
between guys never last long.

64
00:03:58,250 --> 00:03:59,750
So don't take it too seriously.

65
00:04:00,917 --> 00:04:03,875
Why won't you listen to us?

66
00:04:07,083 --> 00:04:08,893
- How about meeting in front of the
station at 11 tomorrow? - Yeah! Sounds good!

67
00:04:08,917 --> 00:04:10,637
- Let's not meet up today.
- Yeah... okay.

68
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,458
(What if we get exposed?)

69
00:04:26,583 --> 00:04:29,643
1. Reactions from others and psychological burden 2.
The general situation in Japan 3. Foreseeable risks.

70
00:04:29,667 --> 00:04:31,167
We have to be careful.

71
00:04:38,125 --> 00:04:41,805
"A secret code just for the two of us" "Confirming
our feelings without anyone else knowing."

72
00:04:44,375 --> 00:04:45,958
A secret code?

73
00:05:05,167 --> 00:05:06,167
This is it.

74
00:05:12,458 --> 00:05:13,708
No good.

75
00:05:14,958 --> 00:05:16,208
What's wrong?

76
00:05:17,917 --> 00:05:19,167
The zipper is broken.

77
00:05:20,958 --> 00:05:23,208
Ah, it's completely busted.

78
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:24,813
The whole thing needs to be replaced.

79
00:05:24,917 --> 00:05:26,042
Seriously?

80
00:05:26,167 --> 00:05:28,375
Senpai, do you know where they sell them?

81
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,917
You can get one at a craft store.

82
00:05:30,042 --> 00:05:32,101
Over by the shopping
street in front of the station.

83
00:05:32,125 --> 00:05:34,042
Someone should know.

84
00:05:34,333 --> 00:05:35,542
Ah.

85
00:05:38,583 --> 00:05:39,125
Sui-senpai.

86
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:39,667
Oh.

87
00:05:39,792 --> 00:05:41,250
I'm off to my training then.

88
00:05:41,375 --> 00:05:42,559
- Good luck.
- I'm heading out.

89
00:05:42,583 --> 00:05:43,792
Take care.

90
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:46,417
Hey, Sui.

91
00:05:46,542 --> 00:05:47,000
Yeah.

92
00:05:47,125 --> 00:05:49,458
Kurobe ran into a little trouble.

93
00:05:49,583 --> 00:05:51,125
Looks like his zipper broke.

94
00:05:51,333 --> 00:05:52,583
Could you come over for a sec?

95
00:05:52,708 --> 00:05:53,917
Sure.

96
00:05:55,042 --> 00:05:56,875
Sui, didn't you go to
a craft store recently?

97
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:57,833
Take him there, will you?

98
00:05:57,958 --> 00:05:58,583
Huh? Ah?

99
00:05:58,708 --> 00:05:59,125
Eh?

100
00:05:59,542 --> 00:06:01,167
Perfect timing.

101
00:06:01,458 --> 00:06:02,458
Let's go.

102
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:03,417
I'm counting on you.

103
00:06:03,542 --> 00:06:04,542
Yeah.

104
00:06:14,292 --> 00:06:16,292
Ah, so this is broken.

105
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:18,458
You really liked this one, too.

106
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:21,958
Sorry about this.

107
00:06:22,083 --> 00:06:24,208
Hmm... it's fine, no worries.

108
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,208
Let's get ready and head out.

109
00:06:26,708 --> 00:06:28,500
I'll go get ready, wait for me a sec.

110
00:06:36,417 --> 00:06:38,500
Hmm... is it this one?

111
00:06:40,875 --> 00:06:42,333
I think this works.

112
00:06:42,667 --> 00:06:44,333
Let's go with this one then.

113
00:06:45,583 --> 00:06:47,000
Thanks.

114
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:02,292
Senpai.

115
00:07:02,417 --> 00:07:03,583
Look.

116
00:07:08,375 --> 00:07:09,708
This looks like Harutora.

117
00:07:09,833 --> 00:07:12,500
Huh? Isn't it a bit too big?

118
00:07:34,542 --> 00:07:36,782
(2. The general situation in
Japan 3. Foreseeable risks)

119
00:07:48,125 --> 00:07:49,417
How about this one?

120
00:07:51,583 --> 00:07:53,042
I think it's really cute.

121
00:07:53,375 --> 00:07:54,583
Really?

122
00:07:54,708 --> 00:07:56,167
Then this...

123
00:08:19,292 --> 00:08:20,542
I'm sorry.

124
00:08:21,625 --> 00:08:22,875
Why?

125
00:08:23,958 --> 00:08:26,292
We are dating, right?

126
00:08:28,583 --> 00:08:30,083
Well, yeah.

127
00:08:31,500 --> 00:08:33,042
How should I put this...

128
00:08:34,167 --> 00:08:38,875
When I think about someone
from school possibly seeing us,

129
00:08:39,792 --> 00:08:41,417
I get a little... scared.

130
00:08:46,292 --> 00:08:47,542
I'm sorry.

131
00:08:51,292 --> 00:08:56,330
It's been so long since we finally got the
chance to spend time together like this.

132
00:09:05,042 --> 00:09:06,250
Here.

133
00:09:08,500 --> 00:09:09,583
Huh?

134
00:09:14,458 --> 00:09:16,333
If we can't hold hands,

135
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:19,250
Just pretend this is me.

136
00:09:23,833 --> 00:09:25,083
Why?

137
00:09:26,875 --> 00:09:28,458
Because your hands are freezing.

138
00:09:33,167 --> 00:09:34,542
Thanks.

139
00:09:37,542 --> 00:09:39,083
Since we're already out,

140
00:09:39,208 --> 00:09:40,667
let's look around a bit more.

141
00:09:40,792 --> 00:09:41,875
Yeah.

142
00:09:45,792 --> 00:09:47,375
If it isn't Sui!

143
00:09:49,250 --> 00:09:50,875
Whoa! You scared me.

144
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,018
We haven't seen each other
since middle school, right?

145
00:09:52,042 --> 00:09:54,333
Uh... yeah.

146
00:09:54,458 --> 00:09:55,958
What's with that reaction?

147
00:09:56,083 --> 00:09:57,542
It's me, Hikaru.

148
00:09:57,667 --> 00:09:58,667
Did you forget?

149
00:09:58,708 --> 00:10:01,083
No way, of course I remember.

150
00:10:03,167 --> 00:10:04,833
Ah, hello.

151
00:10:04,958 --> 00:10:08,167
Sui and I were in the same class
for three years in middle school.

152
00:10:08,292 --> 00:10:10,208
I'm Takahashi Hikaru.

153
00:10:10,542 --> 00:10:12,708
And you are?

154
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:14,667
I'm...

155
00:10:14,792 --> 00:10:16,083
He's my junior.

156
00:10:16,792 --> 00:10:19,500
My old dorm roommate, Harutora.

157
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:25,250
Oh, so you live in a dorm.
No wonder I never see you back home.

158
00:10:25,375 --> 00:10:27,208
I haven't been back much lately.

159
00:10:28,292 --> 00:10:30,000
Do you remember that guy?

160
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:31,726
Matsushita, the one who
took care of the animals.

161
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:33,042
Ah... that brings back memories.

162
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:34,375
Doesn't it make you nostalgic?

163
00:10:34,500 --> 00:10:36,460
I ran into him
back home a while ago.

164
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:41,708
Well, I'll see you around.

165
00:10:41,833 --> 00:10:42,833
Bye.

166
00:10:47,792 --> 00:10:49,542
Ah, sorry.

167
00:10:49,667 --> 00:10:51,833
I totally left you out just now.

168
00:10:53,208 --> 00:10:56,458
Senpai, you seemed a bit
different than usual just now.

169
00:10:57,375 --> 00:11:01,375
Yeah, he's just a regular friend.

170
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,792
But you looked really panicked.

171
00:11:05,042 --> 00:11:07,125
Uh... no I didn't.

172
00:11:08,958 --> 00:11:12,333
Is he really just a regular friend?

173
00:11:24,125 --> 00:11:25,375
I'm sorry.

174
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:34,417
Actually... he's the guy I had
a crush on in middle school.

175
00:11:36,417 --> 00:11:38,958
But it was really only for a short while.

176
00:11:39,542 --> 00:11:42,292
Now I'm completely over him.

177
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:48,375
You only introduced me as
your old roommate and junior.

178
00:11:59,167 --> 00:12:00,542
I'm sorry.

179
00:12:01,333 --> 00:12:04,292
It'd be a hassle if rumors started
spreading back home, right?

180
00:12:16,125 --> 00:12:17,333
Hikaru.

181
00:12:18,875 --> 00:12:20,250
Oh, Sui.

182
00:12:20,375 --> 00:12:21,375
What's up?

183
00:12:24,542 --> 00:12:25,792
Um...

184
00:12:32,708 --> 00:12:33,958
Earlier...

185
00:12:34,333 --> 00:12:36,083
The guy I was with...

186
00:12:37,833 --> 00:12:41,458
He's... he's my boyfriend.

187
00:12:43,417 --> 00:12:44,417
Huh?

188
00:12:47,583 --> 00:12:49,417
My boyfriend.

189
00:12:58,125 --> 00:13:00,917
Hmm...

190
00:13:01,042 --> 00:13:04,958
I kind of figured it
was something like that.

191
00:13:05,083 --> 00:13:08,958
You never really showed much interest
in girls back in middle school anyway.

192
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:10,208
Yeah.

193
00:13:12,042 --> 00:13:13,958
Thanks for telling me.

194
00:13:15,792 --> 00:13:20,042
Um... I actually haven't
told my parents yet.

195
00:13:20,167 --> 00:13:21,417
Okay, okay.

196
00:13:21,542 --> 00:13:23,042
I won't tell anyone.

197
00:13:23,167 --> 00:13:24,417
Don't worry.

198
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,792
Thank you.

199
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,042
Hurry back to him.

200
00:13:30,458 --> 00:13:31,458
Yeah.

201
00:13:31,500 --> 00:13:32,500
See you.

202
00:13:39,833 --> 00:13:41,417
I finally said it.

203
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:55,542
I'm sorry.

204
00:13:58,708 --> 00:13:59,917
Harutora.

205
00:14:10,333 --> 00:14:12,208
After we parted ways, Senpai,

206
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:18,875
I had to keep myself
busy just to calm down.

207
00:14:23,625 --> 00:14:24,917
It was really hard.

208
00:14:28,417 --> 00:14:30,708
It was unbearable.

209
00:14:33,333 --> 00:14:34,958
Where did you go in this heavy rain?

210
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,333
I went for a run.

211
00:14:39,375 --> 00:14:41,292
What exactly happened?

212
00:14:41,917 --> 00:14:43,477
You've been acting really weird lately.

213
00:14:44,917 --> 00:14:46,708
Are you gonna die if you stop moving?

214
00:14:49,792 --> 00:14:51,167
Of course not.

215
00:14:52,042 --> 00:14:53,708
You worry too much.

216
00:14:54,667 --> 00:14:56,187
Is it wrong for me to worry about you?

217
00:14:58,500 --> 00:15:00,333
I know how hard you work.

218
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:03,138
And I know how much you love basketball.
That's why I'm saying this.

219
00:15:03,208 --> 00:15:04,583
Idiot.

220
00:15:20,125 --> 00:15:22,167
Being apart from you, Senpai...

221
00:15:23,042 --> 00:15:24,917
I really can't do it.

222
00:15:27,125 --> 00:15:28,792
If I don't keep moving,

223
00:15:29,833 --> 00:15:31,375
I'll die.

224
00:15:38,875 --> 00:15:40,417
When I was sad,

225
00:15:47,958 --> 00:15:51,083
just hearing you say "Welcome home"
made me feel so warm.

226
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:53,750
And it helped me push through.

227
00:16:01,250 --> 00:16:03,375
Even on the day we lost the game,

228
00:16:05,875 --> 00:16:09,292
You didn't say anything,
you just stayed by my side.

229
00:16:13,583 --> 00:16:15,583
And when you purposely
slept on the floor...

230
00:16:18,542 --> 00:16:21,000
I was so happy you
took care of me like that.

231
00:16:26,792 --> 00:16:28,458
I don't want to be apart from you.

232
00:16:36,708 --> 00:16:38,167
I see...

233
00:16:42,958 --> 00:16:48,000
I didn't realize Hyou were hurting
so much you could barely hold on.

234
00:16:48,375 --> 00:16:50,333
I suddenly feel so loved.

235
00:16:53,292 --> 00:16:56,333
Sorry, why did I just spill my guts?

236
00:16:57,083 --> 00:16:58,083
No...

237
00:16:58,583 --> 00:16:59,667
It's okay.

238
00:16:59,792 --> 00:17:01,417
I like you just the way you are, Senpai.

239
00:17:05,625 --> 00:17:06,917
Is it just me?

240
00:17:09,208 --> 00:17:10,542
Huh?

241
00:17:11,167 --> 00:17:12,708
What about you, Harutora?

242
00:17:13,375 --> 00:17:15,255
Why don't you ever tell
me how you really feel?

243
00:17:15,875 --> 00:17:17,083
Nothing...

244
00:17:17,208 --> 00:17:20,417
It's nothing. Don't worry about me.

245
00:17:20,542 --> 00:17:24,000
You're putting your own
problems aside again.

246
00:17:25,958 --> 00:17:28,000
I have to get things done first.

247
00:17:31,042 --> 00:17:32,708
But normally,

248
00:17:34,667 --> 00:17:36,507
You should take care
of yourself first, right?

249
00:17:39,875 --> 00:17:41,292
But...

250
00:17:42,333 --> 00:17:45,958
If I say childish things,

251
00:17:46,792 --> 00:17:49,042
I'm afraid I'll bother you, Senpai.

252
00:17:52,375 --> 00:17:53,375
Huh?

253
00:17:57,917 --> 00:17:59,292
Harutora.

254
00:17:59,875 --> 00:18:01,500
You're probably...

255
00:18:03,250 --> 00:18:06,458
not as mature as you think you are.

256
00:18:08,625 --> 00:18:09,917
What?

257
00:18:10,042 --> 00:18:12,958
Because you fly off the handle so easily.

258
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,458
I thought I was pretty mature.

259
00:18:22,458 --> 00:18:25,333
After all, I've always taken
care of my younger siblings.

260
00:18:26,875 --> 00:18:29,958
You're kidding, right? Seriously?

261
00:18:32,333 --> 00:18:34,042
I'm so crushed.

262
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
No way...

263
00:18:50,208 --> 00:18:51,958
It's okay to be a kid.

264
00:18:54,417 --> 00:18:55,667
Huh?

265
00:18:57,833 --> 00:19:02,625
Aren't we just starting
to slowly become adults?

266
00:19:05,375 --> 00:19:06,735
Just starting... to become adults?

267
00:19:10,708 --> 00:19:12,167
Harutora.

268
00:19:12,875 --> 00:19:15,000
Harutora, let's play!

269
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:16,476
Let's go to the park! To the park!

270
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:18,542
- Let's go, Harutora!
- Okay...

271
00:19:19,167 --> 00:19:24,667
I've always felt
that I had to act like a big brother.

272
00:19:27,458 --> 00:19:29,042
Like feeling lonely,

273
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:34,792
Or wanting to be spoiled...

274
00:19:37,667 --> 00:19:39,333
I always thought.

275
00:19:40,875 --> 00:19:44,417
Keeping those things to myself
meant I was being sensible.

276
00:19:46,833 --> 00:19:48,375
Harutora.

277
00:19:48,875 --> 00:19:49,875
So...

278
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:53,833
It's okay to say it out loud, right?

279
00:19:55,708 --> 00:19:57,042
Huh?

280
00:20:01,833 --> 00:20:03,208
I really...

281
00:20:20,542 --> 00:20:22,542
...have been so lonely all this time.

282
00:21:37,417 --> 00:21:38,792
(You can do it!)

283
00:21:38,917 --> 00:21:40,250
This...

284
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:44,375
Hold on...

285
00:21:49,583 --> 00:21:52,833
I thought it looked
great when I first made it.

286
00:21:53,458 --> 00:21:56,917
But now that I'm actually giving it to you,
I feel like it's not good enough.

287
00:22:02,458 --> 00:22:04,750
Is that why you went to the craft store?

288
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:06,333
Uh...

289
00:22:06,458 --> 00:22:09,208
I was originally afraid of our
relationship being exposed.

290
00:22:09,333 --> 00:22:12,458
I saw online that you can confirm
your feelings without letting others know.

291
00:22:12,583 --> 00:22:16,125
By making a secret code
just for the two of us.

292
00:22:17,333 --> 00:22:18,542
Look.

293
00:22:18,792 --> 00:22:22,625
Even if we're apart,
our hearts are still with each other.

294
00:22:25,333 --> 00:22:28,958
Sorry, that sounds a
bit too heavy, doesn't it?

295
00:22:33,083 --> 00:22:34,083
Not at all.

296
00:22:39,833 --> 00:22:41,583
I'll cherish it for the rest of my life.

297
00:23:57,583 --> 00:23:58,903
(This drama is purely fictional.)
